@startuml
' Rendered by scripts/build-diagrams.sh. Edit this file, never the SVG beside it.
' The colours, the fonts and the transparent ground come from palette.iuml.
!include palette.iuml

' What earns this picture is not the order of the states, which one sentence
' holds. It is the edge that runs backwards: a lot's lessons reach the next lot
' through a document rather than through somebody's memory, and that loop is the
' thing prose spells out worst.
'
' Entirely grey, on purpose. Nothing here is an owner or a refusal, which is what
' colour is for in this set, so it carries none.
'
' The board columns are inside the state labels rather than in notes. A note
' carrying a sentence drifts from the paragraph beside the image; two words in a
' box cannot.
'
' "one or more pull requests" rather than a branch in the picture. A card can ship
' stacked, and the number is decided once, when the pull request opens, so drawing
' the two outcomes as separate paths would give a reviewer's judgement call the
' weight of a state. The card is still the unit; only the delivery can split.
set separator none
hide empty description

state "Coarse intention" as Intention
state "Sketch\n(Backlog)" as Sketch
state "Specification\n(Todo)" as Spec
state "Merged" as Merged
state "card-management.md" as Doc

Intention --> Sketch : filed
Sketch --> Spec : **the lot opens**\nthe card is rewritten
Spec --> Merged : one card,\none or more\npull requests
Merged --> Doc : what the lot taught
Doc --> Spec : shapes the next\nrewrite
@enduml
